DermViT web app
===============

This app is MIT-licensed (LICENSE). It runs a quantized Vision Transformer model and uses
resampling logic derived from the projects below.

The model: Skin Mole ViT ONNX (MIT) & Skin_Cancer-Image_Classification (Apache-2.0)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The app downloads model_quantized.onnx (models/dermvit.manifest.json) from:
  https://huggingface.co/sazio/skin-mole-vit-onnx (commit 25be9e61a71125de9502648c1f6adceb7a882637)

Modifications relative to upstream weights: exported to ONNX and dynamically quantized to
8-bit weights (model_quantized.onnx, 86,993,703 bytes) by sazio under the MIT License from
Anwarkh1/Skin_Cancer-Image_Classification (https://huggingface.co/Anwarkh1/Skin_Cancer-Image_Classification),
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, which fine-tunes google/vit-base-patch16-224-in21k
(Apache License, Version 2.0) on the HAM10000 dataset (Tschandl et al., Scientific Data 2018).
The full text of the Apache License, Version 2.0 ships in LICENSE-APACHE-2.0 beside this file.

Strictly for research and educational use only; uncalibrated softmax scores are not a medical
device or clinical diagnosis.

Pillow bilinear resampling (MIT-CMU)
------------------------------------
resizeRgbaPillowBilinear in src/core/vit.js follows the scale-dependent separable triangular
(bilinear) resampling of Pillow's src/libImaging/Resample.c (https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow).

